00:32:52.170 --> 00:32:53.800
How tight do you work, how close

00:32:53.800 --> 00:32:55.303
do you work with your guests?

00:32:57.050 --> 00:32:58.420
Can you just talk about that, please?

00:32:58.420 --> 00:32:59.253
- Sure.

00:33:00.920 --> 00:33:03.180
We have an alum and a student.

00:33:03.180 --> 00:33:07.740
And so, I work, I usually take
the first stab at the script,

00:33:07.740 --> 00:33:09.370
and then I share it with the student.

00:33:09.370 --> 00:33:12.803
And then I sit with that
student, and I walk them through,

00:33:12.803 --> 00:33:14.960
I actually have them
talk through the intro

00:33:14.960 --> 00:33:18.410
and outro with me, just so
they feel comfortable with it.

00:33:18.410 --> 00:33:20.660
I have them go through
almost every question.

00:33:21.740 --> 00:33:23.640
I'd say half of my students,
half of the students

00:33:23.640 --> 00:33:26.220
I worked with have been very proactive,

00:33:26.220 --> 00:33:28.800
and have asked a lot
of their own questions.

00:33:28.800 --> 00:33:31.749
I'd say the other half
didn't do that, at all.

00:33:31.749 --> 00:33:33.150
(person chuckling)
Yeah.

00:33:33.150 --> 00:33:34.450
That's just the way it is.

00:33:36.610 --> 00:33:39.120
The prep work, the in-person
prep work was really helpful.

00:33:39.120 --> 00:33:41.580
However, a lot of them are not
used to being in the studio,

00:33:41.580 --> 00:33:44.620
and so, it took, you
know, we usually allow

00:33:44.620 --> 00:33:47.290
for about an hour and a
half from start to finish,

00:33:47.290 --> 00:33:49.290
even though the podcast
itself, the final product

00:33:49.290 --> 00:33:51.970
is only 20 minutes, there's
an hour and a half there.

00:33:51.970 --> 00:33:53.530
And so, by the end of the conversation,

00:33:53.530 --> 00:33:54.780
the student is warmed up.

00:33:55.760 --> 00:33:58.640
We usually go back and
rerecord the intro/outro.

00:33:58.640 --> 00:34:01.940
I see Guy nodding, yeah,
people, it takes awhile for us

00:34:01.940 --> 00:34:03.580
to get comfortable on...

00:34:04.720 --> 00:34:06.347
Yeah, does that answer your question?

00:34:06.347 --> 00:34:07.917
- Yes, yes, thank you.
- Okay, great.

